.#-----------------------------------------------------
.input|xwiki/2.1
.# Standalone code macros located in table cells are rendered as code spans since Markdown table cells can only
.# contain inline content. The language is lost since Markdown has no syntax to specify the language of a code span,
.# and line endings are replaced by spaces (as for verbatim). Consecutive code spans are separated by a space so that
.# they're not read back as a single code span. See code11.test for the parsing of the generated Markdown.
.#-----------------------------------------------------
|=a|=b
|x|(((
{{code language="java"}}
int i = 0;
int j = 1;
{{/code}}
)))
|y|(((
{{code}}a`b{{/code}}

{{code language="none"}}c{{/code}}

{{{d}}}
)))
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|markdown/1.2
.#-----------------------------------------------------
|  a  |            b            |
| --- | ----------------------- |
|  x  | `int i = 0; int j = 1;` |
|  y  |     ``a`b`` `c` `d`     |
